{"strongs": "H1471", "word": "גּוֺי", "translit": "goy", "root": "גוה", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "nation, people", "definition": "גּוֺי 561 noun masculine Gen 12:2 nation, people (Late Hebrew id. Gentiles , Phoenician גו community , , Sabean גו id. , DHM ZMG 1883, 348 ) — ׳ ג Gen 12:2 + 121 t.; suffix 1 singular גּוֺיִ Zeph 2:9 , גּוֺיֶ֑ךָ Ps 106:5 , גּוֺיֵךְ Kt Ezek 36:13 ; Ezek 36:14 ; Ezek 36:15 ( Qr wrongly גּוֺיַיִךְ compare Co , who strike out v Ezek 36:15 ); plural גּוֺיִם Gen 10:5 + 410 t. + Qr Gen 25:23 ; Ps 79:10 ( Kt גיים ) + 6 t. Ezekiel (variant reading emended Co ); construct גּוֺיֵי Gen 18:18 + 8 t., גּוֺיֵ 2Chr 32:13 ; Ezra 6:21 (compare Baer's notes); suffix גּוֺיֵהֶם Gen 10:5 ; Gen 10:20 ; Gen 10:31 ; Gen 10:32 — 1. nation, people Gen 10:5 (twice in verse); Gen 10:20 ; Gen 10:31 ; Gen 10:32 (twice in verse) (all P ) +; Isa 2:2 ; Isa 2:4 (twice in verse) = Mic 4:2 ; Mic 4:3 (twice in verse); Job 12:23 (twice in verse); Job 34:29 ; Prov 14:34 כֹּל גּוֺיֵי הָאָרֶץ Gen 18:18 ; Gen 22:18 ; Gen 26:4 (all J ); Deut 28:1 . \\ \\ a. specifically of descendants of Abraham, גּוֺי גָּדוֺל Gen 12:2 compare Gen 18:18 (both J ), גּוֺיִם Gen 17:6 , הֲמוֺן גּוֺיִם Gen 17:4 ; Gen 17:15 (all P ); of Sarah גּוֺיִם Gen 17:16 ( P ); of Ishmael גּוֺי Gen 21:13 , גָּוֺי גָּדוֺל v Gen 21:18 (both E ), גּוֺי גָּדוֺל Gen 17:20 ( P ); of Jacob גּוֺי וּקְהַל גּוֺיִם Gen 35:11 ( P ), גּוֺי גָּדוֺל Gen 46:3 ( E ); of Ephraim ׳ מְלֹא הַגּ Gen 48:19 ( J ); of Moses גּוֺי גָּדוֺל Exod 32:10 ( J ) compare Num 14:12 ( J ) Deut 9:14 of Jacob and Esau as two nations Gen 25:23 ( J ). \\ \\ b. definitely of Israel Exod 19:6 ( קָדוֺשׁ ׳ גּ ) Exod 33:13 (both J E ), Deut 4:6 ( הַגּוֺי הַגָּדוֺל הַזֶּה , said by heathen compare v Deut 4:7 v Deut 4:8 ) see also v Deut 4:34 , Deut 26:5 compare Ps 33:12 ; Ps 83:5 (said by enemies) Jer 31:36 ; Jer 33:24 ; Ezek 37:22 in narrative Josh 3:17 ; Josh 4:1 ; Josh 5:8 ( J E ), v Josh 5:6 ( D ), Josh 10:13 (in poetry, no article); of Israel and Judah as two nations Ezek 35:10 (said by heathen) Ezek 37:22 of Judah Isa 26:2 ; Isa 26:15 (twice in verse); compare Isa 58:2 ; Isa 60:22 ; Mic 4:7 once my people Zeph 2:9 (|| עַם ); thy people Ps 106:5 (i.e. of ׳ י ), compare also Ezek 36:13 ; Ezek 36:14 (read Kt ); especially of Israel and (or) Judah as sinful, rebellious Deut 32:28 ; Judg 2:20 ; Isa 1:4 ; Isa 10:6 ; Jer 5:9 ; Jer 5:29 ; Jer 7:28 ; Jer 9:8 ; Jer 12:17 ; (strike out ᵐ5 Co ) Hag 2:14 ; Mal 3:9 . — Note. This definite reference to Israel and (or) Judah is comparatively rare; in Hexateuch not P (yet see Gen 17:4 ; Gen 17:5 ; Gen 17:6 ; Gen 17:16 ; Gen 35:11 P ); seldom in exile & post-exile prophets; not Chronicles — \\ \\ c. usually of non-Hebrew peoples Exod 9:24 ; Exod 34:10 ( J E ) Lev 25:44 ( H ) Num 14:15 ( J ) Deut 15:6 (twice in verse); 1Kgs 5:11 ; 1Chr 14:17 ; 1Chr 16:20 ; Isa 11:10 ; Isa 11:12 + often; opposed to Israel as ׳ עם י 2Sam 7:23 ; 1Chr 17:21 (twice in verse) etc., see עם , compare also Num 23:9 note especially גְּלִיל הַגּוֺיִם Isa 8:23 circle or district of the nations (see גָּלִיל ); also ׳ חֲרשֶׁת הַגּ Judg 4:2 ; Judg 4:13 ; Judg 4:16 Charosheth of the nations , & מֶלֶךְ גּוֺיִם לְגִלְגָּ֖ל Josh 12:23 king of nations (peoples, tribes) belonging to Gilgal ( ᵐ5 Di to the district , i.e 'Galilee'); especially of these peoples as heathen: idolatrous Lev 8:24 ; Lev 8:28 ( P ) Lev 20:23 ( H ) 1Kgs 14:24 ; 2Kgs 17:8 ; 2Kgs 17:11 ; 2Kgs 17:15 ; 2Kgs 17:26 ; 2Kgs 17:29 (twice in verse); 2Chr 28:3 ; 2Chr 32:13 +, Ezra 6:21 ; Ezek 5:6 +; hostile Gen 15:14 ( J ) Lev 26:33 ; Lev 26:38 ; Lev 26:45 ( H ) Deut 4:27 ; Deut 9:4 ; Deut 9:5 ; Deut 18:9 ; 1Chr 16:35 ; Jer 5:15 ; Ezek 4:13 + often Jeremiah Ezekiel, etc.; in simile Ezek 20:32 ; Ezek 25:8 sometimes || עַם Ps 33:10 ; Ps 33:12 ; Isa 11:10 ; Jer 6:18 , see also Isa 2:2 ; Isa 2:4 compare with Mic 4:1 ; Mic 4:3 . 2. figurative of swarm of locusts Joel 1:6 of all species of beasts Zeph 2:14 . 3. גּוֺיִם Gen 14:1 ; Gen 14: